# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules (Netlify-compatible syntax).
#
# 1) API proxy — REQUIRED for production login.
#    Replace YOUR-API-HOST with the deployed backend host (e.g. the Render or
#    Railway URL) and uncomment the line. With this rule the frontend uses
#    same-origin /api/* and no CORS override is needed.
#
# /api/*    https://YOUR-API-HOST/api/*    200

# 2) SPA fallback: serve the app shell for client-side routes (deep links such
#    as /login hard-load correctly). Existing static assets take precedence.
/*    /index.html    200
